    "description": "A checkout screen in a retail application manages shipping details, payment selection, validation errors, a busy indicator, and retry behavior. Every user action currently updates several controls independently, so a payment timeout can leave the screen showing both a spinner and an editable form. The CheckoutFeature must expose one immutable snapshot containing a discriminated phase, the entered data, field errors, and pending operation details. Gestures such as selecting a shipping method, submitting the address, retrying payment, and returning to review are represented as explicit values. A pure transition function accepts the previous snapshot and one action and returns the next snapshot; rendering cannot write state. Unit tests must replay sequences such as an expired card followed by replacement details without constructing controls, and the action history must support an audit log. The same feature will later be rendered by the mobile application and a headless preview.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how the checkout screen will represent all user interactions and derive one consistent, immutable screen snapshot through testable transitions.",
    "notes": "Model-view-intent fits because gestures become explicit values reduced by a pure transition function into one immutable snapshot with replayable tests; bloc and model-view-viewmodel are the near-miss siblings and container-component supports the feature boundary."
  },
